{"name":"Resort White","hex":"#f4f1e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"resort","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where people go for recreation, especially one with facilities such as lodgings, entertainment, and a relaxing environment.","Recourse, refuge (something or someone turned to for safety)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have recourse (to), now especially from necessity or frustration.","To fall back; to revert."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resort"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Resort","blocks":[{"text":"A resort is a self-contained commercial establishment that aims to provide most of a vacationer's needs on the premises. Services include food, drink, accommodation, sports, entertainment and shopping. A hotel is frequently a central feature of a resort and the term resort may be used for a hotel that provides an array of entertainment and recreational activities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Pyramid_resort_jasper.JPG/330px-Pyramid_resort_jasper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resort"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Overview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_%2820210907124718%29.jpg/500px-Overview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_%2820210907124718%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Overview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_%2820210907124718%29.jpg/1280px-Overview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_%2820210907124718%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Overview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_%2820210907124718%29.jpg/500px-Overview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_%2820210907124718%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Universal Beijing Resort","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOverview_of_Universal_CityWalk_Beijing_(20210907124718).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Happy_Life_Entrance.JPG/500px-Happy_Life_Entrance.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Happy_Life_Entrance.JPG/1280px-Happy_Life_Entrance.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Happy_Life_Entrance.JPG/500px-Happy_Life_Entrance.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Entrance of an all-inclusive resort in Egypt","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w